# LumiThink R1-08 single-host production configuration template (issue #20).
#
# Deployment model: systemd restricted process (deploy/lumithink.service) with
# an EnvironmentFile at /etc/lumithink/lumithink.env — root-owned, mode 0600,
# readable only by root (the unit drops privileges itself). NEVER commit real
# values; this template documents shapes only. Secrets NEVER enter Git or
# ordinary logs (lib/server/secrets-registry.ts + audit redaction; dirty-marker
# tests enforce it).

# --- Node runtime -------------------------------------------------------------
NODE_ENV=production
# The app listens on LOOPBACK ONLY (the reverse proxy terminates TLS on 443).
PORT=3000
NEXT_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1

# --- Guardian / admin access codes (R1-08 real credentials) -------------------
# Both variables are a PAIR: setting exactly one fails the boot (fail-closed).
# 12-128 chars, no whitespace, never the published synthetic demo codes.
# The values are hashed (SHA-256) at composition; the raw values are never
# logged, echoed or persisted. Rotation: replace both values + restart.
# LUMITHINK_GUARDIAN_ACCESS_CODE=<generate: openssl rand -base64 18>
# LUMITHINK_ADMIN_ACCESS_CODE=<generate: openssl rand -base64 18>

# --- Encrypted runtime snapshot (R1-08 encrypted backup) ----------------------
# AES-256-GCM key, EXACTLY 64 hex chars (32 bytes). Give ONE of:
#   LUMITHINK_SNAPSHOT_KEY          (inline; least preferred — prefer the file)
#   LUMITHINK_SNAPSHOT_KEY_FILE     (controlled mount, e.g. /etc/lumithink/snapshot.key)
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
# LUMITHINK_SNAPSHOT_KEY_FILE=/etc/lumithink/snapshot.key
# Snapshot file (state dir must be writable by the service user, 0750).
# LUMITHINK_SNAPSHOT_PATH=/var/lib/lumithink/snapshot.bin
# Snapshot cadence in ms (confirmed mutations always snapshot immediately).
# LUMITHINK_SNAPSHOT_INTERVAL_MS=60000
# Normally leave at 0/absent. The one-shot post-restore replay request is a
# SELF-CLEARING marker file: deploy/restore.sh touches
# <snapshot-dir>/restore-replay.pending and the runtime consumes (deletes)
# it after the one replaying boot. This env var is an EXPLICIT per-boot
# override ONLY: leaving it at 1 replays (purges everything created since
# the previous restart) after EVERY restart. restore.sh neutralizes any
# leftover =1 it finds.
# LUMITHINK_SNAPSHOT_RESTORE_REPLAY=0

# --- Explicitly NOT here ------------------------------------------------------
# Model provider keys: the app never reads provider credentials at startup.
# The default provider is the in-process Mock (zero egress). Real-provider
# activation requires the independent data-egress review (issue #14 note);
# its key would be request-time injected per MODEL_GATEWAY.md, never here.
